okay let's cut to the chase rayleigh  is a goddamn legendary character that is  oozing charisma  authority and mystery like treble the  snort  a character that is respected by all and  has been the main reason that luffy is  now able to challenge  actual yonko and is back on track to  becoming pirate king  after the most traumatic moment in his  life  and so even though we actually don't  know all too much about his past  i want to use this chance to not only  discuss rayleigh's character and his  role in the story  but also delve a bit deeper into the  classic trope of the mentor  and how if used correctly it can enhance  the fabric of a story  significantly oh yeah and why the hell  is he called the dark king  this is the story of the dark king  silver's  rayleigh  [Music]  first of all can we all acknowledge just  how fantastic rayleigh's introduction  was in the story  out of all the great ones we've gotten  i'm thinking kaido  katakuri or emu this might have actually  been my  favorite one and by that i mean the  entire sequence  it's simply done fantastically  especially in the anime  there is no music just the slave  auctioneer  suddenly collapsing then we just see  this giant sitting there and  holy damn this huge ass guy must have  done something right  but he turns around calls out the old  man sitting next to him for  using something called haki and then  this  this is just the right way to reveal an  epic character like this  that right there has a real shock effect  and the way that rayleigh then enters  the hall later  takes a look at the scene deduces what  happens before  knocking out all the guards how could  you not be intrigued by this mysterious  old man that we now know was the right  hand of the pirate king himself  now rayleigh's name has actually two  sources of inspiration  one is so walter rayleigh an english  16th century explorer and privateer  and the other is a phenomenon known as  rayleigh scattering rayleigh scattering  refers to the scattering of light off of  the molecules in the air  thus changing its wavelength for example  it's light hitting the molecules in our  atmosphere that give us  a blue sky so rayleigh literally  scattering kizoru's light attacks  seems to be a science pun by oda i guess  now the silver in his name of course is  a running theme within the roger pirates  with gold roger  silva's rayleigh and skopper gibany  kevin  personality wise as most of the former  roger pirates we've met so far  roger shanks odin and with the obvious  exception of buggy  rayleigh is an extremely eccentric  charismatic  and joyful person that seems to be  enjoying life to its fullest  and since the roger pirates in many ways  seem to have been quite similar to the  straw hats in terms of their crew  dynamics  it comes as no big surprise that  rayleigh gets along with all of them  quite perfectly and even more so is  immediately likable for us readers as  well  after all this guy has the exact same  values and approach to life  as our heroes but more powerful  mature and confident  [Music]  and the detail that i personally found  really interesting in this context is  that rayleigh as a character  shares a lot of characteristics with  both zorro  and sanji now hear me out just like  zorro  rayleigh is the first mate of the roger  pirates the  right hand of the pirate king and the  first person recruited  both are powerful swordsmen that are  only second to the captain  in terms of strength and just like zorro  rayleigh also has a scar above his eye  has a bit of an alcohol problem and just  as zorro manages to get  lost a lot rayleigh seems to have a  tendency to get shipwrecked as  happens on his way to amazon lilly and  after roger's death where he is saved by  hachi  and of course both of them seem to enjoy  a good battle  [Music]  now on the other hand just like sanji  the first thing rayleigh says  is how much he loves women before  showing us his swordman skills he  actually stops kizuru with  a quite sanji-esque kick also as we see  in the auction house he shares sanji's  cunningness and tendency to go on small  infiltration missions  in fact he actually lets himself get  captured on purpose to steal money from  the slave auction that he had lost  while gambling sanji and zorro  no wonder you can't help but find this  man absolutely awesome now in terms of  his role in the story  rayleigh in many ways fits the  archetypical trope of the mentor  pretty much perfectly the mentor  typically is an experienced advisor and  confidant for the protagonist  that passes on his knowledge and wisdom  so that people can live better lives and  society in general can improve  this character not always but very often  comes in the form of the wise old man or  woman  that is better skilled faster and more  experienced than their students and now  pass these traits onto them at this  point in time they might have grown too  old or too fragile for the tasks or  have their own job to do famous examples  of this trope include yoda in star wars  or tony stark in avengers endgame or to  go more into anime  biscuit in hunter hunter or almighty in  boku no hero  their role is to introduce a new skill  and or set of  ideas and values often hoping to pass  the torch  because they know that their role in the  world is slowly coming to an end  and of course most of the time expect  them to have the same elderly but  powerful look  associated with the grandpa gods  i think you will agree that rayleigh  hits this description  pretty perfectly though compared to some  other manta figures he doesn't have to  die to get their disciple on their feet  we're talking gandalf  dumbledore or jiraya here  for luffy this push is replaced by ace's  death  a small twist on the trope here  i got all now what does this mental role  mean for his relationship with luffy  rayleigh is pretty much the closest  thing that luffy could ever get to being  mentored by roger himself  rayleigh is a relic of the pirate king's  era someone who is respected by everyone  even marines like garb or even kizuru  who doesn't seem to have a lot of  respect for anyone else  [Music]  now based on the stories he's heard from  shanks as well as his personal  experience with luffy  he believes him to be the man that roger  has been waiting for  in other words the man he started the  great pirate era for  in the first place  [Music]  luffy wears his former captain's hat has  a similar  quirky crew and most importantly he has  the exact same dream as roger  though we as an audience still don't  know what that dream is  and so i think it's no coincidence that  rayleigh thinks of roger's last words  after luffy leaves  [Music]  luffy has literally inherited raj's will  and  thus roger didn't die now obviously  after the events at zabaodi and  especially marine ford  rayleigh is fully aware that luffy won't  be able to continue his journey into the  new world at the level that he's  currently at  and so i'm not sure if you remember this  it's actually rayleigh that proposes and  sets up the time skip and decides to  teach luffy as much as he can in two  years  so he actually has a chance against the  monsters waiting in the new world  as a result not only does he pass down  his own knowledge and skills onto him  but also is the one to mentally help him  recover from his trauma  and rekindle his belief in himself and  his ability to protect his crew  and yet in the manner of any good mentor  despite being enormously strong and  respected  rayleigh's time is over and the fact  that despite someone as strong as him  being around  the world still being as messed up as it  is also serves to show us just  how powerful this system is and how  difficult it is to actually change the  worlds  okay so that's all nice and well but  let's talk about the elephant in the  room  why is this man called the dark king  there have been a number of speculations  about this but there are two things here  that i want to highlight  one is the actual meaning of the  japanese world  meo if you watch too much anime like  i do you might know the word mao which  means  demon king or the devil mayo on the  other hand  is the literal japanese name for pluto  or  if you prefer greek or latin hades  the king of the underworlds now please  feel free to theorize as to what this  might mean in the comments  i'd love to hear your ideas as for me  the quite obvious meaning here is that  rayleigh  especially as a user of congress hockey  was  pretty much a king himself one of the  strongest people in the world  the fact that this is obviously not an  epithet he picked for himself  suggests to me that he was seen as the  king in roger's shadow  almost as powerful almost as dangerous  but since raja was the one who shown the  brightest  rayleigh was the dark king  now i'm just gonna assume you haven't  seen all of my analysis videos  yet so please click here to check out my  playlist  also i wanted to use this moment to say  thank you to all my patrons and channel  members  you guys really make this all possible  if you want to become part of the  channel get  early access to all my videos and other  perks all while supporting my work here  i invite you to become a channel member  or check out my patreon page  thanks for
 

